# Documentation and Verification

## Documentation

- Document meaningful implementation changes.
- Never fabricate completed work. If something was not tested, say so explicitly.
- Record errors encountered and how they were fixed.
- Record important architectural decisions and their reasons.
- Keep `PROJECT_AUDIT.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md`, and `FINAL_PROJECT_REPORT.md` accurate when those files exist.

## After meaningful implementation

- Run the appropriate lint checks.
- Run type checking when available.
- Run the production build.
- Run relevant tests.
- Verify affected routes and APIs, and authentication/authorization behavior.
- Verify all supported languages, RTL and LTR layouts, and both Light and Dark modes.
- Do not claim something works unless it was actually verified.
- For web UI changes, verify in the browser (or the closest substitute) before declaring the task complete.
